@startuml
title C4 Level 3 - Seller Component Diagram

skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #4B4B4B
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #F9F9F9
skinparam PackageBorderColor #4B6F91
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F3F8FC
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6A6A6A

left to right direction

actor "User\n(Seller)" as Seller

package "Backend API" {

  component "server.js" as Server
  component "sellerRoutes.js" as Routes
  component "authMiddleware.js" as AuthMiddleware
  component "sellerController.js" as Controller

  package "Seller Controller Functions" {
    component "sellerCreateProduct()" as CreateProduct
    component "getSellerAnalytics()" as SellerAnalytics
    component "updateSellerProduct()" as EditProduct
  }

  component "Prisma Client" as Prisma

  database "PostgreSQL" as DB

  package "Prisma Models" {
    component "User" as UserModel
    component "Product" as ProductModel
    component "OrderItem" as OrderItemModel
    component "Order" as OrderModel
    component "Review" as ReviewModel
  }
}

' External request flow
Seller --> Server : HTTP request
Server --> Routes : mounts router at /api/seller

' Route middleware flow
Routes --> AuthMiddleware : router.use(verifyToken, isSeller)
AuthMiddleware --> Prisma : prisma.user.findUnique()
Prisma --> DB

' Auth details
AuthMiddleware --> UserModel : checks user exists,\nisBanned = false,\nrole = SELLER

' Route to controller flow
Routes --> Controller : calls controller functions

' Controller function mapping
Controller --> CreateProduct : POST /product
Controller --> SellerAnalytics : GET /analytics
Controller --> EditProduct : PUT /product-edit

' Mounted API endpoint notes
note right of Routes
Declared in sellerRoutes.js:
POST /product
GET  /analytics
PUT  /product-edit

Mounted API paths:
POST /api/seller/product
GET  /api/seller/analytics
PUT  /api/seller/product-edit
end note

' Seller role note
note left of Seller
Seller is not a separate model.

Seller is represented as:
User.role = SELLER
end note

' Create Product data flow
CreateProduct --> Prisma : prisma.product.create()
CreateProduct --> ProductModel : creates Product

note bottom of CreateProduct
Creates a new Product with:
- title
- description
- price
- category
- fileUrl
- sellerId = req.user.id
- status = PENDING
end note

' Edit Product data flow
EditProduct --> Prisma : prisma.product.findUnique()
EditProduct --> ProductModel : finds Product by id
EditProduct --> Prisma : prisma.product.update()

note bottom of EditProduct
Update flow:
1. Find Product by id
2. Validate product exists
3. Check ownership:
   product.sellerId == req.user.id
4. Update fields
5. Reset status to PENDING
end note

' Analytics data flow
SellerAnalytics --> Prisma : prisma.product.findMany()
SellerAnalytics --> ProductModel : filters by sellerId
ProductModel --> OrderItemModel : includes orderItems
OrderItemModel --> OrderModel : includes order
OrderModel --> UserModel : includes buyer
ProductModel --> ReviewModel : includes reviews
ReviewModel --> UserModel : includes reviewer

note bottom of SellerAnalytics
Analytics reads seller-owned products:

Product
  -> OrderItem
      -> Order
          -> Buyer/User

Product
  -> Review
      -> Reviewer/User

Only COMPLETED orders are counted
for sales and earnings.
end note

' Model relationships
UserModel --> ProductModel : User.products\nsellerId
UserModel --> OrderModel : User.orders\nbuyerId
UserModel --> ReviewModel : User.reviews\nuserId

ProductModel --> OrderItemModel : Product.orderItems
ProductModel --> ReviewModel : Product.reviews

OrderModel --> OrderItemModel : Order.items

' Database access
ProductModel --> DB
UserModel --> DB
OrderItemModel --> DB
OrderModel --> DB
ReviewModel --> DB

@enduml
